-- #1351's graph, re-pointed here from test/must_fail_fixtures/ when its pin drained.
-- Two UNRELATED interfaces share the bare method name `mth` at DIFFERENT dispatch
-- argument indices (IA at 0, IZ at 1), IZ carries the program's only impl, and
-- `fmodI.mth` is a standalone with the same bare name -- which is load-bearing, not
-- decoration: `methodDispatchIdx`'s only reader is gated on `standaloneValuesRef`, so
-- WITHOUT a standalone shadow the bare-name dispatch-index table is never read at all
-- and the graph is immune to the defect it is meant to exercise.
--
-- Neither interface is nameable here: the entry imports both modules but binds only
-- `af` and `zf`. So `mth` is not a shadow in this module and the occurrence is the
-- standalone this module explicitly imported: 99, on every ordering.
import fmodI.{mth}
import amodI.{af}
import zmodI.{zf}

main = println (mth "abc" 5 + af 0 + zf 0)
